\begin_layout Standard
It is also possible to build one's own physical controllers out of hardware components such as sliders,
 buttons,
 potentiometers,
 or even more sophisticated sensors (e.g.
 LSM9DS1 or BNO055).
 A small inexpensive microcontroller such as a Raspberry Pi Pico W can then format the data into an OSC message and send it through a wired or wireless connection.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The OSC protocol uses a heirarchical address space in which each message includes an address pattern that identifies its destination,
 within a tree-like namespace (somewhat like a heirarchical filesystem structure).
\begin_inset Foot
status open

