\begin_layout Subsection
Basic Attack Demonstration
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As proof-of-concept,
 I simulated a trivial attack using two Raspberry Pi Pico Ws without any security mechanism.
 The victim simply sent OSC messages containing MIDI notes that produced a two-octave C Major arpeggio on the receiving end through a simple Max/MSP patch.
 The attacker sent random MIDI values on the same port as the victim,
 dramatically disrupting the arpeggio.
 The MIDI notes were shown on a standard musical staff:
