\begin_layout Subsection
Performance
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
I did an analysis of latency by making a parallel branch of the code.
 Latency was measured in two ways:
 first as a round-trip value using only Python,
 and second as a gateway processing overhead on the Mac (receiving end).
 The rount-trip method was chosen because it was not possible to synchronize clocks on the Raspberry Pi Pico W and the Mac.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Discussion
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The current weakness is that a longer OSC payload is not supported,
 as the OSC string is limited to 28 bytes.
 But it would be a fairly easy matter to adjust this in the code for version 2.0.
\end_layout

